{
  "name": "cloud_volume_fill",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "§25c (issue #144): the raymarch's FILL cost, at the zoom where cloud covers most of the frame. Split off from cloud_volume_perf, which establishes the whole-map case, because the two want opposite things from the camera and neither can be answered by the per-patch table -- §25c's cost is 192 volume fetches per fragment, so it lands in frameMs and scales with covered screen area, and the C# it adds is eight uniform writes per sheet that the analyzer correctly reports as free. Camera anchored, not merely zoomed: LookAt with a zoom alone leaves the position free, the view drifts between windows, and both the captures and the coverage they were supposed to establish become pictures of a scrolling map. Read the per-row MAX before believing any average: this box shares its memory with other work, and a window carrying a several-hundred-millisecond max inside a trivial postfix has measured a system stall, not a renderer.",
